    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18987" root="سجل" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَجَنْجَلٌ</span></b>  <i>A mirror:</i> (S, K:) or <i>a Chinese
mirror:</i> (MA:) [said to be] a Greek word (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُومِىٌّ</span>),

(S, K,) arabicized: (S:) and some say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَجَنْجَلٌ</span>.
(Az, TA.) [Pl., accord. to Freytag, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَنَاجِلُ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And (assumed tropical:)  <i>Pieces such as are termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَبَاجِلُ</span>, <i>of silver;</i>
(K, * TA;) as being likened to the mirror. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <i>Gold.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <i>Saffron.</i> (K.)

